The X11 host follows the toplevel when GDK does not: after a fullscreen or maximize change
the host's size is compared with the X window's for two seconds; on a mismatch GTK is asked
for a frame, and if GDK still disagrees the host takes the X size and the CEF children are laid
out again. Seen on mutter when a maximized window went fullscreen (the toplevel grew by the
title bar's height, GDK kept the old size). Applied by scripts/prepare-runtime-cef.sh.
Reported upstream as tauri-apps/tauri#16480; drop the patch when a released runtime has it.

diff -ruN rt7-range/src/platform/linux/window.rs /home/develop/projects/dla-launcher/tauri3/vendor/tauri-runtime-cef/src/platform/linux/window.rs
--- a/src/platform/linux/window.rs	2026-11-07 08:04:10.560200939 +0100
+++ b/src/platform/linux/window.rs	2026-11-07 08:02:56.921507615 +0100
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@
